//! The per-unit proof bridges (R19, plan step 18), one Rust module per ported unit.
//!
//! **This file is written once and is never edited by a port task.** The module list below is
//! generated by `build.rs` from the files actually present in `src/proof_units/`, so a port task
//! adds its unit by creating three new files and touching nothing that another port task also
//! writes:
//!
//! - `cxx/proof_units/<unit>.h` -- the shim's C++ declarations; `#include`s its own
//!   `cxx`-generated header, `"slic3r-ffi/src/proof_units/<unit>.rs.h"`.
//! - `cxx/proof_units/<unit>.cpp` -- the shim's C++ definitions (proof path 1), or the
//!   translation unit that `#include`s the vendored `.cpp` whole (proof path 3).
//! - `src/proof_units/<unit>.rs` -- one
//!   `#[cxx::bridge(namespace = "slic3r_ffi::proof_units::<unit>")]`.
//!
//! `<unit>` is the unit's `port/manifest.tsv` `target module` file stem (`object_id` for
//! `crates/slic3r-objectid/src/object_id.rs`), so the shim's name is derivable from the manifest
//! row and two units can never pick the same file name. `build.rs` globs both directories, adds
//! every `src/proof_units/*.rs` to `cxx_build::bridges(...)` and every
//! `cxx/proof_units/*.cpp` to the shared `cxx_build::Build` -- which carries
//! `-ffp-contract=off` and the whole include set -- and writes the `#[path]`-ed module list this
//! file includes. There is no shared list, no shared C++ file and no shared `pub use` block to
//! append to, because every one of those was a merge conflict between the hundreds of port
//! branches built side by side (`docs/PORTING.md`, "Decisions recorded on 2026-11-25").
//!
//! A port task's proof reaches a unit's bridge through `slic3r-proof`, which re-exports this
//! module (`slic3r_proof::proof_units::<unit>::<fn>`); it never depends on `slic3r-ffi` itself
//! and never adds a dependency to any `Cargo.toml`.

// The `#[path]`-ed `pub mod` line for every `src/proof_units/*.rs`, generated by `build.rs` into
// `OUT_DIR` on every build. `include!` is what makes the list derived rather than hand-edited;
// `just port-check` runs `rustfmt --check` over the globbed bridge files directly, because
// `cargo fmt` cannot follow an `include!` and so never reaches them.
include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/proof_units_mods.rs"));
